"""E57 job 1280 (recompute oracle): LIGHT pilot-informed registration text, v11 (server repo copy; DRAFT; text only, no new .md file). Analysis code: e57_1280_analyze.py. External record = a SIGNED tag pushed to a private remote repository after v11 is complete and re-checked and before the first confirmatory seed is run; the checker (check_external_record) compares the tag signature, the tagged scripts and the REMOTE (server-side) time with the oldest result file. DELETED from earlier versions: the A / B / A-prime hash freezes, the public-commit timing evidence, the predictive-probability futility rule, the interim look and its boundaries, the blind failure-classification procedure, the SESOI derivation. Nothing in this text was written after opening any 1280, instrumentation or auxiliary-seed output (none exists)."""
import re
PLACEHOLDERS=['instrumentation k (from seeds 91..94; needs Hans GPU sentence)','private registry repository name (REGISTRY_REPO) and the push of the signed tag (Hans confirms; the origin remote of this working tree is PUBLIC)']
REGISTRATION_V11=r"""1 STATUS AND TERMS. This is a PILOT-INFORMED registered analysis: the thresholds were fixed after the 3-seed pilot (job 1279), see item 13. Unqualified pre-registration wording is not used; the term is 'pilot-informed registered analysis'. A result that is not detected is NOT evidence that there is no leak. External record: a signed tag on the commit that contains this text and e57_1280_analyze.py is pushed to a private remote repository AFTER v11 is complete and re-checked and BEFORE the first confirmatory seed is run; the checker verifies the signature, that the tagged scripts equal the working-tree scripts, and that the remote (server-side) time of the tag is older than the oldest confirmatory result file.
2 DESIGN. n = 30 confirmatory seeds (101..130), one fixed-sample analysis; no interim look, no stopping, no extension; unit = seed. Instrumentation seeds 91..94 (variance components at k = 8 only) and the auxiliary NATS 16->128 seeds 901..908 (descriptive only) are separate from the confirmatory seeds and never enter them. Every arm and every seed result is reported.
3 CLAIMS AND GATES (table CLAIMS_TABLE; one-sided, alpha = .05 each; intersection-union hierarchy 3a -> 3b -> 3c, size <= .05, NOT multiplicity-corrected). E-form: E = NLL(blocked) - NLL(not blocked); E_cache = a - nc, E_rec = b - c, E_mask = recomputed band NLL - recomputed natural NLL (nat/token); margins G = M_NATMASK - M_NATS, H = M_RECOMP - M_NATS (nat/fact). Contrasts T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec, T_Q = E_rec - .7 E_mask, L_F = H - .7 G; placebo: PLd = M_RECOMP_PL - M_NATS with one-sided upper confidence bound < delta_PL = .25 nat (absolute). Gates 2a (E_rec > 0, mean >= .25), 2b (E_mask > 0, mean >= .10), 2c (G > 0). Verdict 4 CACHE SUFFICIENT = gate 2a and T_R > 0, a separate claim at its own .05. Flags (not claims): F_LOW, H_GEN, HALF_PL, ANOMALY, G_PRACTICAL.
4 TESTS AND WORDING. Each test is run twice: the seed-paired t test (df = 29) and the exact sign-flip test. 'Significant' is written only when BOTH reject. When the t test rejects and the exact test does not, the wording is 'supported, distribution-sensitive'. When only the exact test rejects there is no claim (flag SIGNFLIP_ONLY). A step that does not reject is written 'not detected', which is not evidence of absence. HOLM: the intersection-union claim is not corrected; in addition the four component tests (T_R leak, T_Q, L_F, placebo) are Holm-adjusted over four tests at level .05, using for each test the LARGER of its two p-values, max(p_t, p_exact); a component without a Holm-adjusted rejection that is reported outside the intersection claim is labelled EXPLORATORY. The wording of every outcome is drafted in OUTCOME_PHRASES before the results exist.
5 SIGN-FLIP: EXACT COMPUTATION AND LIMITS. The exact one-sided p = P(S >= S_obs), S = sum of s_i x_i with s_i = +-1 uniform, is computed over ALL 2^30 sign vectors by meet-in-the-middle (two halves of 15 signs, sorted sums, binary search): CPU benchmark (benchmark_exact, n = 30, 48-core server, e57_1280_exact_bench.json): 0.0125 s per test, 0.100 s per analysis of 8 exact tests, 7.9 MB for the two cached sign matrices, peak RSS 102 MB, so the exact computation is feasible and the Monte Carlo fallback is not used; the exact routine refuses n > 32. If this were infeasible the pre-specified fallback is a Monte Carlo sign-flip with >= 1e6 sign vectors, numpy PCG64 seed 20261112, p = (1 + count) / (1 + 1e6). LIMITS: (a) the test is exact only under symmetry of the seed contrast about 0 under H0; it tests symmetry about zero, not mean zero, so under a skewed contrast it can reject for a reason other than a nonzero mean; in a simulation of skewed contrasts (shifted lognormal, sigma 1.5, mean shift .35, n = 30, 3000 datasets) the t test alone rejected in 1 and the exact test alone in 9, which is why an exact-only rejection is never a claim; (b) the smallest attainable p is 2^-30, so resolution is not a constraint at n = 30; (c) ties and exact zeros are counted as at least as extreme (conservative); (d) it is a sensitivity partner of the t test, not a distribution-free replacement of the estimand.
6 SEEDS AND FAILURES. A failure is a seed whose run diverges or yields a non-finite value. At most 3 failed seeds are replaced, in order, by 131, 132, 133; every failure is reported with its seed and kind; beyond the cap the analysis uses the remaining seeds and reports n. A failure is never classified by its outcome (fill_seeds raises on any other reason).
7 LOWER BOUND ON n AND MISSING SEEDS. n_min = 27 (Hans 2026-11-11). With fewer than 27 seeds the whole result is labelled EXPLORATORY. Whenever seeds are missing (n < 30) a WORST-CASE sensitivity is reported: every missing seed is imputed as ZERO EFFECT (all contrasts and gate quantities 0) and the analysis is repeated with n = 30; the verdict is called robust to missing seeds only if its level is unchanged (final_report).
8 SESOI. SESOI_fact = .5 nat/fact, FIXED by decision (Hans 2026-11-11), irrespective of the pilot uncertainty; there is no coefficient, no derivation from the auxiliary seeds and no replacement rule; nat/token has no SESOI. SESOI enters no test. G_PRACTICAL = TRUE only when the one-sided 95% lower bound of G is >= .5 nat/fact. delta_PL = .25 nat absolute.
9 CONFOUND TABLE (CONFOUND_TABLE): placebo and oracle arms are matched in masked length (exactly) and position (mean masked position within 64 tokens) and checked for attention mass; attention mass is NOT matched and is reported as a covariate per seed (confound_check); a length or position mismatch is reported with the seed. Rationale for 64 tokens: it is one quarter of the 256-token band, so the oracle and its placebo spans stay in the same band quarter and their distance to the read position differs by at most a quarter of the band; this is a design choice, not a measured equivalence margin.
10 GENERALITY BRIDGE (one candidate, BRIDGE_CANDIDATE): public-QA write stream NATS vs NATMASK, exploratory, not part of the 3c claim.
11 POWER AND GPU TIME AT n = 30: POWER_NOTE (rows by margin-SD assumption with its source marked; t only and t-and-exact; numbers in e57_1280_power_n30.json), GPU hours in GPU_NOTE; values >= .9999 are printed '>=.9999'; no claim of achieving a power target is made.
12 1284 IS A SEPARATE FAMILY: seeds 201..220, its own alpha = .05 one-sided, primary RECOMP-ORACLE - RECOMP-PL, key secondary HALF-PL - HALF; it is not pooled with 1280 and shares no seed (checked).
13 DISCLOSURE. Pilot (job 1279, seeds 62..64, K0 = 0, exploratory, 2 degrees of freedom, excluded from the confirmatory set): X_ORACLE .076 / .065 / .079; X_MASK .337 / .367 / .383; PLACEBO - NATS +.096 / +.036 / -.003 (mean +.043, SD .050); RAND - NATS +.048 / -.010 / -.022. Thresholds fixed after the pilot: .25, .10, .8, .7, .7, .3, SESOI .5, 1.2, 3 of 32 unmatched, delta_PL .25, n = 30, n_min = 27, the cap of 3 replacements, the 64-token position tolerance. Expectation (not a prediction): E_cache is small relative to E_rec (pilot .07 vs .36), so if gate 2a passes the leak direction follows almost automatically; the T_R leak result is therefore not counted as independent confirmation. Power statements are scenario estimates.
14 DELETED FROM EARLIER VERSIONS: A / B / A-prime hash freezes, public-commit timing evidence (replaced by the signed-tag external record), predictive-probability futility, interim look and boundaries, blind failure classification, informative-failure sensitivity, SESOI derivation and its fallback. Archived in git (commits up to 09793bf408e7a3afd165a487050aa3c698d015c9)."""
CLAIMS_TABLE=[
 dict(id='gate 2a',claim='the recomputed blocking effect E_rec is certified',estimand='E_rec (nat/token)',test='t and exact sign-flip, one-sided; mean >= .25',level=.05,gate='-',if_significant='E_rec is certified'),
 dict(id='gate 2b',claim='the recomputed band effect E_mask is certified',estimand='E_mask (nat/token)',test='t and exact, one-sided; mean >= .10',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='E_mask is certified'),
 dict(id='gate 2c',claim='the masked update has a positive margin effect G',estimand='G (nat/fact)',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='G > 0'),
 dict(id='3a',claim='the cached oracle explains less than 80% of the recomputed effect (leak)',estimand='T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec < 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='R-leak'),
 dict(id='3b',claim='3a and the recomputed band effect explains the recomputed oracle effect',estimand='T_Q = E_rec - .7 E_mask > 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a, 2b, 3a',if_significant='R-leak and Q'),
 dict(id='3c',claim='3b and the margin effect follows the masked direction, and the placebo does not exceed .25 nat',estimand='L_F = H - .7 G > 0; PLd upper bound < .25',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a, 2b, 2c, 3b',if_significant='leak confirmed'),
 dict(id='4',claim='the cached oracle is sufficient',estimand='T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec > 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='cache sufficient')]
CONFOUND_TABLE=[
 dict(arm_pair='ORACLE (cached) vs ORACLE-PL',masked='earlier same-fact sentences (oracle) vs other facts sentences (placebo)',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens (one quarter of the 256-token band)',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check'),
 dict(arm_pair='RECOMP vs RECOMP-PL',masked='recomputed oracle band vs recomputed placebo band',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens (one quarter of the 256-token band)',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check'),
 dict(arm_pair='HALF vs HALF-PL',masked='band-256 half oracle (own-fact exposures reopened) vs its placebo',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens (one quarter of the 256-token band)',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check')]
BRIDGE_CANDIDATE=dict(name='public-QA write stream, NATS vs NATMASK (e57_pqa_natmask_run.py)',question='does the masked-direction update effect G found in the synthetic fact worlds also appear on public-QA facts',contrast='G_QA = margin(NATMASK) - margin(NATS) per bundle, one-sided',unit='bundle (5 bundles, 65-version stream); EXPLORATORY: reported with CI, no claim',gpu_time='about 2 h (measured: write job 1268 took 107 min for 5 arms, so about 45 min for 2 arms; read stage about 80 min as in job 1295; to be re-measured)',status='design only; needs Hans GPU sentence')
OUTCOME_PHRASES={
 '3c':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), blocking the earlier same-fact exposure from the update path raised the later-exposure NLL by {E_rec:.3f} nat/token under full recomputation, whereas the cached oracle accounted for only {E_cache:.3f} nat/token (T_R = {TR:.3f}); both the t test and the exact sign-flip test rejected at the one-sided .05 level for every step of the hierarchy, including the margin effect (G = {G:.2f} nat/fact) and the placebo bound (< .25 nat).",
 '3b':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle under-explained the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}) and the recomputed band effect explained it (T_Q), with both the t test and the exact sign-flip test rejecting; the margin and placebo conditions of the full claim were not detected together, so we report the leak mechanism without the margin-level confirmation.",
 '3a':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle explained less than 80% of the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}; t and exact sign-flip both rejected); the band-effect step was not detected, which is not evidence that the band effect is absent.",
 '4':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle accounted for at least 80% of the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}; t and exact sign-flip both rejected), so the stale-cache account is sufficient for this setting.",
 '2a':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the recomputed blocking effect was not detected above .25 nat/token (E_rec = {E_rec:.3f}), the downstream comparisons are therefore not interpreted, and this does not establish that there is no leak.",
 '6':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), no step of the leak hierarchy was detected under both tests; this is not evidence of the absence of a leak, and the effect sizes with their intervals are reported in full.",
 'sensitive':"The {level} result is supported by the t test but not by the exact sign-flip test (supported, distribution-sensitive); we therefore do not describe it as significant.",
 'exploratory':"Because only {n} of 30 planned seeds were available (below the lower bound of 27), this result is exploratory; with the missing seeds imputed as zero effect the verdict level {robust_text}.",
 '1':"The protocol or instrument checks failed in this pilot-informed registered analysis, so the results are reported as exploratory only."}
TERM_RULES=['use "pilot-informed"; never an unqualified "pre-registered"','never write that a result that is not detected shows there is no leak','"significant" only when both the t test and the exact sign-flip test reject; otherwise "supported, distribution-sensitive"; a step that does not reject is "not detected"']
def check_terms(text):
    """returns the list of violations of TERM_RULES in text ('pre-registered' without 'pilot-informed ' directly before it; 'no leak' sentences without a negation; 'not detected' / 'non-significant' / 'not significant' sentences without 'not evidence' or 'does not establish' or 'not interpreted')"""
    v=[]
    if re.search(r'(?i)(?<!pilot-informed )pre-?registered',text):v.append('unqualified pre-registered')
    for sent in re.split(r'(?<=[.;])\s+',text):
        low=sent.lower()
        if re.search(r'\bno leak(age)?\b',low) and not re.search(r"\bnot\b|\bn't\b",low):v.append('no-leak claim: '+sent[:60])
        if re.search(r'non-?significant|not significant',low):v.append('use "not detected": '+sent[:60])
        if re.search(r'not detected',low) and not re.search(r'not evidence|does not establish|not interpreted|not detected together',low):v.append('not-detected without caveat: '+sent[:60])
    return v
POWER_NOTE='fixed n = 30, one-sided .05 per test, scenario E_cache .07, E_rec .30, E_mask .35, G 2.0, H 1.6, PLd 0 (delta_PL .25), margin-family SD in {.05, .225, .45, .90} x rho(G,H) in {0, .7, .9}; SD SOURCES: .05 = PILOT-BASED (SD of the pilot placebo difference PL - NATS, 3 seeds, df = 2), .225 = PILOT-BASED 95% upper confidence limit of that SD (.05 * sqrt(2 / chi2_.05(2)) = .22), .45 = ASSUMPTION (working value, origin not re-derived), .90 = ASSUMPTION (stress case); token-family SDs fixed at the scenario values; N = 1e5 common random numbers (t only) and the first 1e4 with the exact test; result wording: a component or the joint claim below the target is described as not detected at that SD, never as absent. Joint 3c power, t only (rho 0 / .7 / .9): SD .05 [pilot-based]: >=.9999 / >=.9999 / >=.9999; SD .225 [pilot-based upper limit]: .987 / >=.9999 / >=.9999; SD .45 [assumption]: .559 / .864 / .907; SD .90 [assumption]: .110 / .221 / .348; t and exact together differ from t only by at most .004; bottleneck components L_F and the placebo (SD .90: .250-.795 and .437); joint minus product of marginals within .001. The pilot-based rows rest on 3 seeds (df = 2) and are not a basis for the claim that the design is well powered; at the assumed SD .45 the joint claim is detected with probability .56-.91 depending on rho'
GPU_NOTE='GPU hours = seeds x minutes per seed; per-seed minutes are NOT measured for the 1280 branch arms: optimistic 45 / central 60 / pessimistic 90 give 22.5 / 30 / 45 h for n = 30 (15 / 20 / 30 h for the former n = 20); the auxiliary seeds 901..908 (NATS only, about 10 min per arm, about 1.5 h) and the instrumentation seeds 91..94 (4 seeds at k = 8, about 4 h at the central estimate) are extra; the branch-arm timing needs a GPU benchmark and waits for Hans'
def selftest():
    import e57_1280_analyze as A
    assert REGISTRATION_V11.count('\n')==13 and 'pilot-informed' in REGISTRATION_V11 and 'Archived in git' in REGISTRATION_V11 and 'n_min = 27' in REGISTRATION_V11 and 'max(p_t, p_exact)' in REGISTRATION_V11 and 'SESOI_fact = .5 nat/fact, FIXED' in REGISTRATION_V11
    assert check_terms(REGISTRATION_V11)==[],check_terms(REGISTRATION_V11)
    for k,t in OUTCOME_PHRASES.items():
        bad=check_terms(t);assert not bad,(k,bad)
    assert set(OUTCOME_PHRASES)=={'3c','3b','3a','4','2a','6','sensitive','exploratory','1'}
    assert check_terms('The effect was pre-registered.')==['unqualified pre-registered'] and check_terms('This shows there is no leak.') and check_terms('The result was not significant.') and check_terms('The step was not detected.') and not check_terms('The step was not detected, which is not evidence of no leak.')
    assert not check_terms('This is a pilot-informed pre-registered analysis.')
    assert [r['id'] for r in CLAIMS_TABLE]==['gate 2a','gate 2b','gate 2c','3a','3b','3c','4'] and all(r['level']==0.05 for r in CLAIMS_TABLE)
    assert len(CONFOUND_TABLE)==3 and all('confound_check' in r['check'] and '256-token band' in r['position'] for r in CONFOUND_TABLE)
    assert A.P['delta_PL_value']==0.25 and A.P['sesoi_fact']==0.5 and A.P['n_min']==27 and A.SEEDS_1284[0]==201 and len(PLACEHOLDERS)==2
    fm=OUTCOME_PHRASES['3c'].format(n=30,E_rec=0.3,E_cache=0.07,TR=-0.17,G=2.0);assert 'pilot-informed' in fm and not check_terms(fm)
    print('e57_1280_registration selftest ok')
if __name__=='__main__':
    import sys
    if '--selftest' in sys.argv:selftest()
